course: dictionary
lesson: 6942
title: Painkillers: stop the pain, not always the cause
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A painkiller is a medicine that makes pain less strong, or stops it for a while. «Calpol is a brand of paracetamol for children» tells you that paracetamol is a painkiller. Look for clue words: pain, medicine, stops.
explain: Painkillers hide pain, but they do not always cure the problem. «Painkillers block pain signals and lower fever but don't cure the cause.» So a painkiller can help you feel better while your body fights the illness.
explain: Safety comes first. Only take painkillers when an adult gives them to you, and always follow the dose on the label. Too much can be dangerous, so keep all medicines away from small children.
fact: A painkiller makes pain less strong, or stops it for a while.
fact: Paracetamol and ibuprofen are common painkillers.
fact: Painkillers hide pain, but they do not always cure the problem.
fact: Only take a painkiller when an adult gives it to you, and follow the dose on the label.
fact: Too much medicine can be dangerous, so keep all medicines away from small children.
exercise: «Most sore throats get better on their own within about a week; painkillers help meanwhile.» What is a painkiller? | A doctor who checks your ears | A type of virus that causes sore throats | *A medicine that makes pain less strong or stops it for a while | A cold drink that cools your throat
exercise: The label says to follow the dose. Why? | It makes the medicine taste better | Labels are only for shops | *Too much can be dangerous
exercise: Ella has a headache. Her big brother has painkillers. What should she do? | Share them with her little sister | Take them with fizzy drink | *Ask an adult first | Take two tablets to be safe
test: «Painkillers block pain signals and lower fever but don't cure the cause.» What does this tell you? | *Painkillers can hide pain but may not cure the problem | Painkillers always cure the illness | Painkillers are only for bones | Painkillers make you sleep for a week
test: Where should you keep medicines? | In reach of small children | *Out of reach of small children | In a sweet jar | On the kitchen table
exam: Scientists made «a strong painkiller» from cone snail venom. What does painkiller mean? | A type of ice lolly | A snail that stings fish | A tooth full of venom | *Something that makes pain less strong or stops it for a while
